==German==

===Etymology===
From an older word {{term|lass|lass, laß|languid, slothful, idle, weary|lang=de}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|laz|laz|slow, sluggish|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|Germanic|lataz|slow, weary|lang=de}} from {{proto|Indo-European|lad-|slow, weary|lang=de}}. Akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|læt|læt|slow, slack, lax, late|lang=ang}} ({{etyl|en|-}} {{term|late|lang=en}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|𐌻𐌰𐍄𐍃|tr=lats||sluggish, weary|lang=got}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|lassus||tired|lang=la}}. More at [[late]].

